emeOverride_2","displayName":"Select an active power plan","description":"This policy setting specifies the active power plan from a list of default Windows power plans. To specify a custom power plan, use the Custom Active Power Plan setting.\r\n\r\nIf you enable this policy setting, specify a power plan from the Active Power Plan list.\r\n\r\nIf you disable or do not configure this policy setting, users control this setting.\r\n ","categoryId":"290ec637-e780-4e95-9834-6368ac0437d1","baseUri":"./Device/Vendor/MSFT/Policy","offsetUri":"/Config/ADMX_Power/InboxActiveSchemeOverride_2","rootDefinitionId":"device_vendor_msft_policy_config_admx_power_inboxactiveschemeoverride_2","uxBehavior":"toggle","infoUrls":["https://docs.microsoft.com/windows/client-management/mdm/policy-csp-admx-power#admx-power-inboxactiveschemeoverride-2"],"applicability":{"platform":"windows10","technologies":"mdm"},"defaultOptionId":"device_vendor_msft_policy_config_admx_power_inboxactiveschemeoverride_2_0","options":[{"itemId":"device_vendor_msft_policy_config_admx_power_inboxactiveschemeoverride_2_0","displayName":"Disabled","dependedOnBy":[]},{"itemId":"device_vendor_msft_policy_config_admx_power_inboxactiveschemeoverride_2_1","displayName":"Enabled","dependedOnBy":[{"dependedOnBy":"device_vendor_msft_policy_config_admx_power_inboxactiveschemeoverride_2_inboxactiveschemeoverrideenter","required":true}]}]},{"@odata.type":"#microsoft.graph.deviceManagementConfigurationChoiceSettingDefinition","id":"user_vendor_msft_policy_config_admx_power_pw_promptpasswordonresume","name":"PW_PromptPasswordOnResume","displayName":"Prompt for password on resume from hibernate/suspend (User)","description":"This policy setting allows you to configure client computers to lock and prompt for a password when resuming from a hibernate or suspend state.\r\n\r\nIf you enable this policy setting, the client computer is locked and prompted for a password when it is resumed from a suspend or hibernate state.\r\n\r\nIf y